  <data name="About_Tagline.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>A study project on screen sharing.</value></data>
  <data name="About_Description.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Beamcast is a lab: it captures a Windows screen or window straight on the GPU, compresses it with the hardware H.264 or HEVC encoder (VP8 on the CPU as a fallback) and streams it over TCP to anyone holding the invite code. It exists to study codecs, capture and real-time streaming, and as a case study for a separate enterprise application.</value></data>
  <data name="About_Version" xml:space="preserve"><value>Version {0}</value></data>
  <data name="About_CardShareTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Broadcast</value></data>
  <data name="About_CardShareBody.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Pick a screen or window, tune the quality and go live. Capture stays on the GPU and the hardware encoder (H.264/HEVC) compresses it before it goes over TCP.</value></data>
  <data name="About_CardJoinTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Watch</value></data>
  <data name="About_CardJoinBody.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Paste the code, join and watch. Double-click for fullscreen.</value></data>
  <data name="About_CardNetTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Network</value></data>
  <data name="About_CardNetBody.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Works out of the box on the same network. Over the internet, the broadcaster needs to forward the port on the router.</value></data>

  <data name="Title_StudyBadge.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>STUDY PROJECT</value></data>

